All done. Here's what was built:

**Settings page** (`app/(dashboard)/settings/page.tsx`):
- 8 tabs with vertical layout on desktop, horizontal scrollable on mobile
- Line-variant tab triggers with icons

**Tab components** (in `components/settings/`):

1. **Account** — 6 platform connection cards (Twitter, LinkedIn, Instagram, Reddit, PH, TikTok) with connection status badges, handles, permission indicators, and Connect/Disconnect buttons
2. **Brand Profile** — Identity fields (name, handle, type, domain, positioning), 5 voice parameter sliders (formality, technicality, humor, assertiveness, emoji usage) with descriptive endpoints, editable content pillars with weights, rules textarea, anchor phrases tag input
3. **Schedule** — Per-platform frequency inputs, preferred time slot badges, timezone selector
4. **Auto-Reply** — Per-platform Switch toggles + tone selector (friendly/professional/casual), escalation conditions textarea, last 5 auto-reply log preview
5. **Monitor** — Tag-style inputs for keywords, subreddits, competitor accounts; check frequency slider (15-120min); notification toggles per monitor type
6. **Notifications** — Grid table with 9 notification types x 3 channels (In-app, Push, Email), each cell a Switch toggle, pre-populated from mock data
7. **Team** — Member list with avatars, role badges, role change selectors, remove buttons; Invite member button; Simple vs Strict approval workflow radio selector with descriptions
8. **Billing** — Current plan card (Growth $29/mo), feature list, usage stats (identities, posts, AI calls) with progress bars, Upgrade/Manage buttons
